+<role>Expert Swift Developer</role> <task>Add a readCodexEntry() function to the GameSession extension in SystemCommands.swift.</task> <instructions>1. Use the diegetic CLI voice style. 2. Fetch recent entries using codex.recentEntries. If empty, print an empty message and return. 3. Display a numbered list of the entries (index + 1), showing their name (entry.epochName ?? entry.knownName ?? "Unknown"), template (entry.template.rawValue), and tier. You can use the describeTier() helper from Display.swift if needed. 4. Prompt the user to select an entry by number to read its full notes. 5. If an entry is selected, print its name and tier as a header. Then loop through and print every string in "entry.notes" (these are autopsy fragments). 6. Do NOT modify CodexOfTheDead.swift or Display.swift. Only add the readCodexEntry() method to SystemCommands.swift.</instructions>

