+<role>Expert Swift Developer</role> <task>Add an inspectFragment() function to the GameSession extension in InventoryCommands.swift.</task> <instructions>1. Use the diegetic CLI voice style. 2. First check if "inventory.fragments" is empty. If it is, print "  Your satchel contains no fragments." and return. 3. Call "listFragments()" to show the user their fragments. 4. Prompt: "\n  Which fragment do you wish to inspect? (Enter a number)". Read user input and parse it as a 1-based index into "inventory.fragments". 5. If the index is invalid or they dont enter a number, print "  You leave the bone where it lies." and return. 6. If valid, fetch the fragment. Print the header "\n  ── Fragment Details ──". 7. Print the following details on separate lines prefixed with "    ": Type (using describeRemainsType.capitalized), Condition (using describeIntegrity, plus the raw "fragment.integrity.value * 100" as an Int percentage), Era (using describeEra), Domain (raw value capitalized), Affinity (e.g. "Aligned with [X], Opposed to [Y]"), Inscribed Name (if not nil, in quotes). 8. Finally, print Intrinsic Traces (comma-separated list of all tags using "fragment.tags.tags.map { $0.value }") and the Coherence Weight formatted to 2 decimal places using "String(format:)". Do NOT modify Fragment.swift or Display.swift.</instructions>

