+<role>Expert Swift Developer</role> <task>Replace advanceTime() with campMenu() in SystemCommands.swift.</task> <instructions>1. Use the diegetic CLI voice style. 2. Replace the existing `advanceTime()` function with `func campMenu()`. 3. Print `\n  ── Rest & Recovery ──\n  1. Sleep through the night\n  2. Wash and purify\n  0. Cancel`. 4. Read the user input. If 0 or invalid, print `"  You turn back to your work."` and return immediately. 5. If 1 (Sleep): print `\n  You find a safe corner and close your eyes.` and reduce fatigue slightly: `profile.tokens.ritualFatigue = max(0.0, profile.tokens.ritualFatigue - 0.1)`. 6. If 2 (Purify): print `\n  You attempt to wash the ash from your skin.`. Check if `inventory.libations.contains(.water)`. If true, prompt `"  Use water from your satchel for a deeper cleanse? (y/n): "`. If they type "y", remove the first occurrence of `.water` from `inventory.libations`, call `profile.purify(strength: 0.5)`, and print `"  The clean water washes away the unseen weight."`. If they type "n" or dont have water, call `profile.purify(strength: 0.2)` and print `"  You scrub with dry dust. It helps, but only slightly."`. 7. After processing choice 1 or 2, advance the time exactly like the old `advanceTime()` function did: call `clock.advanceForRest(world: &world, sites: &sites, npcs: &npcs)`, check if events are empty (printing `"  The world turns. Nothing of note."` if they are, or calling `processWorldEvents(events)` if not), and finally call `processDirectorEvents()`. 8. Do NOT modify any other files.</instructions>

# 2026-05-02 02:36:09.764755
+<role>Expert Swift Developer</role> <task>Implement the Scavenging Mechanics across the engine and CLI.</task> <instructions>1. In RitualSite.swift, add three new public variables: `var fragments: [Fragment]`, `var artifacts: [LifeArtifact]`, `var memoryTraces: [MemoryTrace]`. Add them to the `init` with default `[]`. 2. In RidgeOfElah.swift, pass the hardcoded arrays to the specific sites in their initializers: pass `battlefieldFragments()` to `battlefieldRidge()`, `telKeshetFragments()` to `telKeshet()`, etc. Pass `starterArtifacts()` to `telKeshet()`. Pass `starterMemoryTraces()` to `nahalCaves()`. Change `RidgeOfElah.createWorld()` to return ONLY `(region: RegionState, sites: [RitualSite])`. 3. In GameSession.swift, update the `GameSession.init()` to handle the new `createWorld()` tuple. Initialize `inventory` with empty arrays for fragments, artifacts, and memoryTraces, but keep the `libations: [.water, .water, .water, .fermentedWine, .fermentedWine]`. Add a switch case for `"search", "scavenge"` that calls `scavengeSite()`. 4. In TravelCommands.swift, implement `func scavengeSite()` inside the `GameSession` extension. If the current site (`sites[currentSiteIndex]`) has any fragments, artifacts, or memoryTraces, append them ALL into `inventory`, clear them from the site, print a diegetic message detailing the counts found, increase `sites[currentSiteIndex].localSuspicion` by 0.3, and advance time using `let events = clock.advanceForCommand(world: &world, sites: &sites, npcs: &npcs)`, then process events. If the site is empty, print `"  You search the area, but the earth yields nothing."`.</instructions>

# 2026-05-02 02:43:34.936397
+<role>Expert Swift Developer</role> <task>Implement the CLI portion of Scavenging Mechanics.</task> <instructions>1. Use the diegetic CLI voice style. 2. In GameSession.swift, update the `GameSession.init()` because `content.fragments`, `content.artifacts`, and `content.memoryTraces` no longer exist on the `content` tuple. Initialize `inventory` with empty arrays `[]` for fragments, artifacts, and memoryTraces, but keep the `libations: [.water, .water, .water, .fermentedWine, .fermentedWine]`. Add a switch case for `"search", "scavenge"` that calls `scavengeSite()`. 3. In TravelCommands.swift, implement `func scavengeSite()` inside the `GameSession` extension. Check if the current site (`sites[currentSiteIndex]`) has any fragments, artifacts, or memoryTraces. If it does, append them ALL into the player`s `inventory`, and then clear those arrays on the site. Print a diegetic message detailing what was found. Increase the site`s `localSuspicion` by 0.3. Advance time by calling `let events = clock.advanceForCommand(world: &world, sites: &sites, npcs: &npcs)`. Process the events via `if !events.isEmpty { processWorldEvents(events) }`. Finally, call `processDirectorEvents()`. If the site is empty, print `"  You search the area, but the earth yields nothing."`.</instructions>
